  "nameStory": "",
  "description": "Chromosera lilacifolia is a small, delicate waxcap mushroom characterized by its distinctive lilac or purple-tinged coloring on the cap and stem. This fungus belongs to the Hygrocybaceae family and is found in mossy, grassy areas throughout New England.",
  "idTips": [
    {
      "label": "Lilac-colored Cap",
      "description": "The cap ranges from pale lilac to purplish, often fading with age, and is typically small (0.5-1.5 cm diameter)",
      "isPrimary": true
    },
    {
      "label": "Waxy Gills",
      "description": "Features characteristic waxy, widely-spaced gills that are pale to whitish, typical of the waxcap family",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Slender Purple Stem",
      "description": "The stem is thin, brittle, and colored similarly to the cap with lilac tones that may fade toward the base",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "Chromosera lilacifolia thrives in moist, mossy grasslands and meadows, preferring areas with rich organic matter and consistent moisture.",
